---
import EdAbstractInstructions from "../../components/forms/preview/examples/EdAbstractInstructions";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="ED Abstract instruction design">
  <div class="grid-container padding-y-4">
    <p class="text-bold text-uppercase font-sans-xs">Draft design · FID 267 v1.1</p>
    <h1>ED Abstract instructions</h1>
    <p class="measure-6">
      Compare the same source wording as plain paragraphs and two semantic lists.
      The single attachment answer stays unchanged. This is an explicit display fixture;
      TypeSpec authoring and the plan contract still need a design decision.
    </p>
    <EdAbstractInstructions client:only="react" />
    <section class="margin-top-5 measure-6">
      <h2>Decisions for review</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Use this narrow section-description extension, or accept plain text? HTML is the candidate here; Markdown authoring remains an alternative.</li>
        <li>Keep all instructions inside the attachment section, with this heading and source wording?</li>
        <li>Retain, translate or omit the legacy empty/uploaded-state messages? They are not part of the permanent introduction.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/HHS/simpler-grants-gov/issues/13000">Issue 13000</a>{" "}
        currently asks for no new UI components. The shared display helper is a proposed scope change;
        this example does not waive that criterion or complete the form migration.
      </p>
      <details>
        <summary>Source notices and boundaries</summary>
        <p>DAT2-0, when empty: “You must attach one and only one file to this page.”</p>
        <p>DAT3-0, after attachment: “You may now Close the Form”.</p>
        <p>DAT4-0, after attachment: “You have attached 1 file to this page, no more files may be added. To add a different file, you must first delete the existing file.”</p>
        <p>
          These are review quotations, outside the form. Existing upload/delete feedback needs
          an explicit disposition; no Close control, context answer or new state framework is proposed.
        </p>
        <p>
          The current library adapter is a temporary frontend copy. Its format pass-through must
          carry into the pending native renderer; a preview here does not prove that convergence.
          Plan-tree ingestion, compiler emission, API registration and XML output remain separate work.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sources:
          <a href="https://apply07.grants.gov/apply/forms/sample/ED_Abstract-V1.1_F267.xls">DAT</a>,
          <a href="https://apply07.grants.gov/apply/forms/readonly/ED_Abstract-V1.1_F267.pdf">PDF</a>,
          <a href="https://apply07.grants.gov/apply/forms/schemas/ED_Abstract-V1.1.xsd">XSD</a>.
          Persistent rows1-1–1-12 provide five general and three research bullets;
          “principals” and the non-electronic note are retained verbatim.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  :global(.ed-instructions-example) {
    max-width: 52rem;
    border: 1px solid #dfe1e2;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  :global(.ed-instructions-example .section-description) {
    color: #1b1b1b;
  }
  :global(.ed-instructions-example .section-description li) {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    :global(.ed-instructions-example) { padding: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
